WEBVTT

00:01:35.740 --> 00:01:37.690
Hime-neetan, I love-love you!

00:01:38.060 --> 00:01:39.580
Kiss!

00:01:40.020 --> 00:01:42.840
Himeno is certainly popular with girls.

00:01:43.210 --> 00:01:44.900
What's wrong with that?

00:01:44.900 --> 00:01:47.920
It's better than getting 
into trouble with boys.

00:01:47.920 --> 00:01:50.140
Of course, since Hime-chan's so pretty,

00:01:50.140 --> 00:01:52.760
I'd think boys won't 
leave her alone, either.

00:01:52.760 --> 00:01:55.340
I'm always nagging Shino,

00:01:55.340 --> 00:01:58.630
so she must love how 
Hime-neetan spoils her.

00:02:00.140 --> 00:02:01.590
Still, though...

00:02:01.590 --> 00:02:04.730
Shino-chan looks just like Himeno 
did when she was little.

00:02:04.730 --> 00:02:06.480
Really? What a lucky break!

00:02:06.480 --> 00:02:09.680
Hey, Shino, you're gonna be 
a beauty when you grow up!

00:02:11.830 --> 00:02:15.140
Now, if she'd just take after her brains,
 too, it'd be perfect.

00:02:15.720 --> 00:02:17.950
I don't know if that'd be for the best.

00:02:17.950 --> 00:02:19.480
What are you talking about?

00:02:19.890 --> 00:02:23.150
If my daughter got into a national 
prep school like yours did,

00:02:23.150 --> 00:02:24.570
what more could I ask for?

00:02:25.470 --> 00:02:27.900
A national school would be a 
lifesaver for our budget!

00:02:28.300 --> 00:02:30.080
Is it that simple?

00:02:30.080 --> 00:02:32.380
<i>If you do go to a good school...</i>

00:02:32.380 --> 00:02:36.010
<i>How could you buy all those books? 
We still have loans to pay off!</i>

00:02:36.940 --> 00:02:40.980
It's best to let kids grow 
up worry-free, I think.

00:02:41.260 --> 00:02:43.630
Only people who have that 
option can say that.

00:02:43.980 --> 00:02:46.070
Want to go to my room?

00:02:49.960 --> 00:02:52.560
The hero returned to his homeland,

00:02:52.560 --> 00:02:54.520
where he drew up a constitution

00:02:54.520 --> 00:02:59.770
and lived a long, democratic lifestyle with 
the former princess and all the animals.

00:03:00.120 --> 00:03:01.560
The end.

00:03:03.620 --> 00:03:05.460
Are you too hot, Shino-chan?

00:03:05.460 --> 00:03:07.190
Nope, I'm not hot!

00:03:07.900 --> 00:03:10.390
You're awfully sweaty, though.

00:03:11.680 --> 00:03:13.880
Why don't we go buy some ice cream?

00:03:13.880 --> 00:03:15.190
Let's go!

00:03:16.200 --> 00:03:21.410
See, short-selling is when you borrow shares,
 sell them, and then buy them back.

00:03:21.410 --> 00:03:22.620
The buy and sell rates—

00:03:22.620 --> 00:03:24.450
Aunt Midoriko— I mean, Sis!

00:03:24.980 --> 00:03:26.620
You'll be here for a while, right?

00:03:26.620 --> 00:03:29.400
Yeah, this will probably 
take another three hours.

00:03:55.570 --> 00:03:58.790
Tama-chan... and your triplet sisters!

00:03:59.470 --> 00:04:01.050
Oh, Kimihara-san.

00:04:01.050 --> 00:04:03.550
I don't often see you outside of school.

00:04:03.550 --> 00:04:06.140
She has big boobies!

00:04:06.140 --> 00:04:08.140
Stop saying boobies!

00:04:06.140 --> 00:04:08.690
Boobies! Boobies! Boobies!

00:04:08.140 --> 00:04:08.680
Girls!

00:04:09.260 --> 00:04:13.330
It's been a while, Chiho-chan, 
Chinami-chan, and Chigusa-chan.

00:04:13.800 --> 00:04:15.890
Hello kiss!

00:04:17.530 --> 00:04:18.540
Kiss!

00:04:18.540 --> 00:04:19.600
No!

00:04:20.440 --> 00:04:23.010
Hime-neetan is my onee-tan!

00:04:23.010 --> 00:04:24.600
I'm the only one who can kiss her!

00:04:27.410 --> 00:04:29.660
Want to kiss our big sister?

00:04:29.660 --> 00:04:30.360
No.

00:04:30.370 --> 00:04:33.370
<b>Pedestrians and 
Bicycles Only</b>

00:04:35.170 --> 00:04:38.870
Now, listen. You only kiss 
people you love-love.

00:04:39.190 --> 00:04:42.120
But we love-love the big onee-chan.

00:04:42.390 --> 00:04:43.560
It's different!

00:04:43.970 --> 00:04:46.220
Hime-neetan loves me most of all!

00:04:46.560 --> 00:04:48.470
So you keep her all to yourself?

00:04:48.780 --> 00:04:50.920
That's not very nice.

00:04:50.920 --> 00:04:51.730
Yeah!

00:04:52.150 --> 00:04:55.980
Our big sister kisses all of us,
 and Sue-chan, too.

00:04:55.980 --> 00:04:57.310
Four times a day!

00:04:57.720 --> 00:04:59.330
A good morning kiss...

00:05:00.110 --> 00:05:02.090
A goodbye kiss...

00:05:02.510 --> 00:05:04.700
A welcome home kiss...

00:05:05.210 --> 00:05:06.730
And a goodnight kiss.

00:05:08.780 --> 00:05:10.740
Wh-What's wrong with that?

00:05:11.680 --> 00:05:14.660
Is the big onee-chan your friend, Nee-chan?

00:05:16.170 --> 00:05:17.240
Yes, she is.

00:05:17.240 --> 00:05:19.740
Does that mean you love-love her?

00:05:19.740 --> 00:05:22.420
Well, I suppose I don't hate her.

00:05:23.310 --> 00:05:26.360
Do you kiss the big onee-chan?

00:05:31.200 --> 00:05:32.320
I do not.

00:05:33.490 --> 00:05:34.720
Why not?

00:05:34.720 --> 00:05:35.840
Because.

00:05:35.840 --> 00:05:39.020
Girls don't kiss each other 
once they've grown up.

00:05:39.020 --> 00:05:40.120
Really?

00:05:40.120 --> 00:05:41.310
It's true.

00:05:48.200 --> 00:05:50.910
Now, this is an unusual combination.

00:05:51.500 --> 00:05:53.010
Your kid sister, Princess?

00:05:53.010 --> 00:05:54.410
She's my cousin.

00:05:55.190 --> 00:05:56.440
And these are...?

00:05:56.440 --> 00:05:58.950
Wow, clone sisters?

00:05:58.950 --> 00:06:00.360
They're my sisters.

00:06:00.360 --> 00:06:01.830
Hello!

00:06:02.290 --> 00:06:04.970
Are you Nee-chan's friends?

00:06:04.970 --> 00:06:06.030
That's right.

00:06:06.030 --> 00:06:08.920
But since you're big, you don't kiss her,
 even though you love-love her?

00:06:09.410 --> 00:06:10.240
Kiss?

00:06:11.450 --> 00:06:14.380
Nee-chan said girls don't 
kiss once they grow up.

00:06:14.380 --> 00:06:16.550
That's not true at all. Watch!

00:06:21.860 --> 00:06:22.880
There, see?

00:06:23.770 --> 00:06:25.590
Don't you, "There, see?" me!

00:06:25.590 --> 00:06:27.210
How could you do that 
in front of children?!

00:06:27.210 --> 00:06:30.690
Don't be such a stiff.
 You're not some old-timey PTA hag.

00:06:30.690 --> 00:06:32.140
Who are you calling a hag?!

00:06:33.250 --> 00:06:34.870
They kissed.

00:06:34.870 --> 00:06:35.960
Forget that!

00:06:38.720 --> 00:06:40.200
Um...

00:06:40.530 --> 00:06:45.460
See? Even when you're big, 
it's good to kiss someone you love.

00:06:45.740 --> 00:06:47.620
So Nee-chan is wrong?

00:06:47.620 --> 00:06:48.710
Yep.

00:06:49.660 --> 00:06:53.760
But... a kiss on the mouth isn't 
for just anyone you love-love.

00:06:53.760 --> 00:06:57.520
That should be saved for 
just one special person.

00:06:59.950 --> 00:07:02.960
Is that something you figure 
out when you grow up?

00:07:02.960 --> 00:07:04.020
Yeah, that's right.

00:07:04.670 --> 00:07:06.450
And pervy things, too?

00:07:06.450 --> 00:07:08.030
Well... Yeah, I guess...

00:07:09.710 --> 00:07:12.120
What? I explained it well.

00:07:12.120 --> 00:07:15.030
Oh, you can still kiss anyone 
you like on the cheek.

00:07:15.030 --> 00:07:16.790
Like this. Watch.

00:07:19.910 --> 00:07:21.900
H-Hey!

00:07:25.400 --> 00:07:28.670
Wait, were we friends?

00:07:28.860 --> 00:07:31.660
Aw, come on. We're besties!

00:07:32.850 --> 00:07:36.480
No! Hime-neetan only love-loves me!

00:07:37.980 --> 00:07:40.530
Okay, I'll just kiss you, then.

00:07:42.660 --> 00:07:44.390
That's enough.

00:07:44.390 --> 00:07:46.040
We're out of time.

00:07:48.330 --> 00:07:50.320
See ya later, kittens.

00:07:50.590 --> 00:07:53.310
Bye-bye, pervy onee-chan!

00:07:56.380 --> 00:07:57.910
Want me to give you a kiss?

00:07:57.910 --> 00:08:01.580
No! I don't love-love you!

00:08:03.320 --> 00:08:04.470
Nee-nee!

00:08:04.470 --> 00:08:06.040
Why not?

00:08:07.820 --> 00:08:08.700
She ran away!

00:08:09.290 --> 00:08:11.050
Don't run away!

00:08:11.050 --> 00:08:12.150
Stop!

00:08:12.150 --> 00:08:13.570
U-Uh...

00:08:13.570 --> 00:08:15.140
Don't worry about it.

00:08:15.910 --> 00:08:18.210
Playing around together will 
help them become friends.

00:08:19.160 --> 00:08:20.460
No!

00:08:20.460 --> 00:08:22.220
Wait up! Wait up!

00:08:25.540 --> 00:08:26.340
What?

00:08:26.800 --> 00:08:30.020
You seem almost like a mom, Tama-chan.

00:08:30.020 --> 00:08:32.230
I guess I'd have to agree with that.

00:08:32.540 --> 00:08:35.450
So don't cause any trouble
in class, all right?

00:08:35.890 --> 00:08:37.700
Uh...

00:08:47.910 --> 00:08:51.350
Aw, and these are your best clothes...

00:08:52.670 --> 00:08:57.140
Looking after small children makes you 
understand the struggles a mother endures.

00:08:57.410 --> 00:08:59.610
Whoa, Tama-chan...

00:09:00.090 --> 00:09:01.420
Are you mad?

00:09:02.060 --> 00:09:03.620
No, I'm not mad.

00:09:08.020 --> 00:09:09.420
Bye-bye!

00:09:09.420 --> 00:09:10.510
See ya!

00:09:10.860 --> 00:09:12.790
I'll give you a kiss next time!

00:09:19.890 --> 00:09:21.700
Did you fall in a ditch or something?

00:09:23.350 --> 00:09:25.500
Weren't you going to the convenience store?

00:09:25.500 --> 00:09:27.990
We ran into a girl from my class.

00:09:27.990 --> 00:09:29.660
Were you making trouble again?

00:09:29.660 --> 00:09:31.740
Um, I'm very sorry.

00:09:31.740 --> 00:09:35.540
Think nothing of it. She can be naughty
for such a shy girl, huh?

00:09:36.070 --> 00:09:39.300
There's no warm bathwater drawn, 
but you can take a shower.

00:09:39.610 --> 00:09:41.670
I'm gonna shower with Hime-neetan!

00:09:46.180 --> 00:09:48.030
Okay, lay your ears down.

00:09:48.030 --> 00:09:49.240
I'm rinsing you off now.

00:09:55.610 --> 00:09:56.890
Am I smelly?

00:09:56.890 --> 00:09:58.950
No, you smell nice.

00:10:00.410 --> 00:10:02.460
I'll wash you too, Hime-nee-tan!

00:10:14.530 --> 00:10:16.470
I'll rinse you off now.

00:10:17.890 --> 00:10:19.300
Am I all clean now?

00:10:19.300 --> 00:10:20.410
Uh-huh!

00:10:24.650 --> 00:10:25.640
Hime-nee, do you...

00:10:26.440 --> 00:10:27.840
make milk?

00:10:28.210 --> 00:10:30.670
No, I can't say I do...

00:10:35.460 --> 00:10:37.340
Hey, Hime-neetan...

00:10:38.410 --> 00:10:43.440
I didn't really understand what the 
two girls who were kissing meant.

00:10:44.000 --> 00:10:45.540
Well...

00:10:46.040 --> 00:10:49.160
I think you will when 
you're a little older.

00:10:49.160 --> 00:10:52.650
When I have big boobies like yours?

00:11:11.000 --> 00:11:12.270
Sorry about that.

00:11:12.270 --> 00:11:13.500
No problem.

00:11:17.400 --> 00:11:19.950
Bye, Aunt Midoriko— I mean, Sis.

00:11:20.800 --> 00:11:25.500
I've been thinking lately that I 
don't mind being called an aunt.

00:11:25.970 --> 00:11:28.090
See you next time, Shino-chan.

00:11:35.070 --> 00:11:37.700
If only you were a boy, Hime-chan...

00:11:38.040 --> 00:11:40.980
I don't think I could give Shino 
to a loli-yuri lover, though.

00:11:42.010 --> 00:11:46.930
<b>Where Do the Little Ones 
Get So Much Vitality?</b>

00:11:42.450 --> 00:11:44.270
Um...

00:11:46.930 --> 00:11:51.940
<b>Regardless of 
the Generation, 
Magical Girls
 Are Popular, Huh?</b>

00:11:46.930 --> 00:11:51.940
<b>Right After This!</b>

00:11:47.680 --> 00:11:51.230
<i>Magical Girl Pretty Horn</i> 
starts right after this!

00:11:52.080 --> 00:11:56.560
Dodgeball, dodgeball, dodgeball, 
dodgeball, dodgeball...

00:11:56.560 --> 00:11:58.380
Dodgeball.

00:11:59.260 --> 00:12:00.570
That's all of them.

00:12:01.540 --> 00:12:05.000
I guess this means we'll be playing 
dodgeball during every free period.

00:12:05.000 --> 00:12:06.540
The majority rules, y'know.

00:12:06.530 --> 00:12:14.380
<b>Nap  Basketball  Dodgeball  Pool</b>

00:12:06.540 --> 00:12:08.440
This time, at least.

00:12:09.060 --> 00:12:13.790
But next time, we'll decide using a method 
that reflects the will of the minority, too.

00:12:13.790 --> 00:12:14.370
What?!

00:12:15.030 --> 00:12:16.690
I won't accept that!

00:12:16.690 --> 00:12:19.970
To deny the majority is to deny democracy!

00:12:23.140 --> 00:12:25.460
Democratic space is distorting!

00:12:29.620 --> 00:12:32.170
Awaken, power of ethics!

00:12:32.420 --> 00:12:34.940
Guide us, law and logic!

00:12:35.270 --> 00:12:39.200
Grant the greatest happiness to 
the greatest number of people!

00:12:48.000 --> 00:12:50.410
Magical Girl Pretty Horn!

00:12:51.410 --> 00:12:53.780
<i>Take this! Ostrakismos!</i>

00:12:53.780 --> 00:12:55.530
Raise your right arm.

00:12:55.210 --> 00:12:58.680
<i>Warped democracy won't work on me!</i>

00:12:55.800 --> 00:12:57.480
Raise your left arm.

00:12:57.480 --> 00:13:00.230
Don't lower your right arm.

00:13:00.790 --> 00:13:03.540
<i>Underwater dodgeball, eh? Now 
that's using your head.</i>

00:13:00.970 --> 00:13:02.710
Raise your tail.

00:13:04.120 --> 00:13:06.810
Is your tail up, Sue-chan?

00:13:04.770 --> 00:13:09.060
<i>Invention is the proof of 
mankind's progress!</i>

00:13:10.340 --> 00:13:12.000
Hey, Chi-chans.

00:13:12.000 --> 00:13:14.910
Huh? Nee-chan, today's Sunday.

00:13:14.910 --> 00:13:16.250
Are you still half-asleep?

00:13:16.250 --> 00:13:17.790
Who are you calling half-asleep?

00:13:18.140 --> 00:13:22.230
I'm going out, so you girls stay 
here and watch the house.

00:13:22.760 --> 00:13:24.150
Aw!

00:13:24.540 --> 00:13:28.250
But we made plans to go out and play, too!

00:13:28.250 --> 00:13:31.070
You know Sue-chan can't 
stay here by herself.

00:13:32.230 --> 00:13:34.660
We'll take Sue-chan with us!

00:13:34.660 --> 00:13:37.520
You can't. She's too weak.

00:13:37.520 --> 00:13:39.720
What if she gets a fever while she's out?

00:13:40.250 --> 00:13:43.260
Hmph! What are we supposed to do, then?

00:13:43.590 --> 00:13:46.050
I told you, you're staying 
here to watch the house.

00:13:46.050 --> 00:13:49.480
Why isn't Dad here, anyway?

00:13:49.800 --> 00:13:51.590
Dad is at work.

00:13:51.590 --> 00:13:54.850
But isn't his work painting pictures?

00:13:55.210 --> 00:13:58.440
He's not getting anywhere when 
he's away all the time.

00:13:58.820 --> 00:14:03.040
Painting is work for his spirit. 
He has a different job for making money.

00:14:03.040 --> 00:14:05.300
That logic doesn't make sense!

00:14:06.110 --> 00:14:09.980
Society doesn't understand it either,
 but that's how it works.

00:14:11.730 --> 00:14:15.370
If he needs money, 
there's some in the offering box.

00:14:15.370 --> 00:14:17.460
That money belongs to the gods.

00:14:18.410 --> 00:14:22.290
Isn't it a grown-up's duty to play 
with their kids on days off?

00:14:22.860 --> 00:14:25.790
I wish I could, but please 
do as I say for today.

00:14:26.020 --> 00:14:29.230
We're in kindergarten, you know!

00:14:29.230 --> 00:14:32.070
You shouldn't make kindergartners 
stay home alone!

00:14:32.070 --> 00:14:35.120
You three are small, 
but you're very trustworthy.

00:14:35.120 --> 00:14:36.410
And there are three of you.

00:14:38.500 --> 00:14:40.220
Okay, fine.

00:14:40.220 --> 00:14:41.310
Have a good time.

00:14:41.680 --> 00:14:43.360
Okay, I'm counting on you.

00:14:44.860 --> 00:14:47.670
We can at least invite 
a friend over, right?

00:14:47.670 --> 00:14:50.010
You can, but just play quietly.

00:14:50.670 --> 00:14:52.020
This house is old.

00:14:57.920 --> 00:15:00.590
Hi, Nacchan? It's Chigusa.

00:15:00.590 --> 00:15:03.570
Our sister is making us stay 
home while she goes out, so...

00:15:03.570 --> 00:15:05.840
Oh, can you? Yeah, come over!

00:15:12.290 --> 00:15:13.430
A-chan?

00:15:13.430 --> 00:15:14.710
Uh-huh. Can you come?

00:15:15.920 --> 00:15:17.960
How many friends are you going to call?

00:15:20.150 --> 00:15:22.460
All right, keep an eye on things here.

00:15:23.460 --> 00:15:25.430
Don't answer the door for 
anyone you don't know.

00:15:25.430 --> 00:15:26.480
We know.

00:15:27.180 --> 00:15:28.490
Have a good time!

00:15:38.620 --> 00:15:40.020
Oh, club work?

00:15:40.020 --> 00:15:41.750
Yeah. You?

00:15:42.310 --> 00:15:43.390
Student council.

00:15:43.390 --> 00:15:44.940
Good luck!

00:15:48.920 --> 00:15:51.060
What club is she in, again?

00:15:51.580 --> 00:15:53.790
Rock, paper, scissors!

00:16:01.510 --> 00:16:02.820
Found you!

00:16:04.380 --> 00:16:05.990
Wait up!

00:16:13.620 --> 00:16:15.500
Sue-chan, are you okay?

00:16:15.500 --> 00:16:16.830
Chi-chan!

00:16:24.390 --> 00:16:27.170
Are you okay? Do you feel sick?

00:16:27.170 --> 00:16:29.780
No. I want to play more.

00:16:29.780 --> 00:16:31.750
You can't. You need to rest.

00:16:33.020 --> 00:16:35.310
I want to play with you...

00:16:36.060 --> 00:16:39.890
This always happens when 
Sue-chan runs around a lot.

00:16:39.890 --> 00:16:41.600
Let's play inside.

00:16:43.820 --> 00:16:45.310
It's 3:00.

00:16:45.910 --> 00:16:48.130
I believe we've discussed 
all there is to discuss,

00:16:48.130 --> 00:16:50.380
so I'd like to take a vote now.

00:16:53.430 --> 00:16:56.600
Wait a second! 
There's still more to talk about!

00:16:56.600 --> 00:17:00.360
Yeah! We need to keep discussing this 
until everyone's in agreement!

00:17:00.660 --> 00:17:04.160
No, we decided in advance 
that if an agreement

00:17:04.160 --> 00:17:06.760
wasn't reached by 3:00, we would vote.

00:17:07.450 --> 00:17:09.330
Now, is everyone ready?

00:17:09.680 --> 00:17:11.840
Isn't that being a bit too bureaucratic?

00:17:11.840 --> 00:17:14.950
You just want to go home, don't you?

00:17:15.910 --> 00:17:17.460
That's right. So what?

00:17:17.850 --> 00:17:19.630
You admit it?

00:17:19.630 --> 00:17:21.000
Hey, come on!

00:17:21.620 --> 00:17:22.840
Listen.

00:17:22.840 --> 00:17:27.270
I've already allowed this debate 
to carve into my private time,

00:17:27.270 --> 00:17:30.150
and I need to be home by 4:00

00:17:30.630 --> 00:17:33.660
to make dinner for my father 
and little sisters.

00:17:34.740 --> 00:17:36.530
Anyone have a problem with that?

00:17:38.540 --> 00:17:39.960
Then let's vote.

00:17:41.370 --> 00:17:44.870
<b>Student Council Office</b>

00:17:44.670 --> 00:17:46.910
Um, Mitama-san.

00:17:44.870 --> 00:17:47.880
<b>Bargain Fair</b>

00:17:48.630 --> 00:17:50.110
Yes? Can I help you?

00:17:50.680 --> 00:17:54.520
You know, I understand what 
you're trying to say,

00:17:54.520 --> 00:17:56.610
and I think you're right.

00:17:56.610 --> 00:18:00.510
But the student council isn't just a job.

00:18:00.510 --> 00:18:02.630
It's more like a club.

00:18:02.960 --> 00:18:06.640
Debates are sort of like a 
page out of our youth...

00:18:07.300 --> 00:18:08.310
And?

00:18:08.740 --> 00:18:12.620
Maybe your sisters could put up 
with you being late for once?

00:18:12.620 --> 00:18:13.470
They can't.

00:18:15.140 --> 00:18:18.580
My grandfather was passionate 
about some martial art.

00:18:18.580 --> 00:18:22.070
He was so stubborn that he never 
gave any thought to his family.

00:18:22.300 --> 00:18:25.070
When he fell into critical condition,

00:18:25.800 --> 00:18:28.340
he called me by my mother's 
name and said...

00:18:29.910 --> 00:18:31.330
"Let's go home."

00:18:32.960 --> 00:18:36.330
Ever since then, I've put my family first.

00:18:36.970 --> 00:18:37.730
Goodbye.

00:18:45.820 --> 00:18:51.340
I think we'll need about thirty years more 
life experience before we can convince her.

00:18:51.340 --> 00:18:55.400
She's never going to get anywhere 
in the real world like that.

00:18:55.680 --> 00:18:57.990
Like you've ever been in the real world.

00:18:58.300 --> 00:18:59.800
Well, it's true!

00:18:59.800 --> 00:19:02.680
For their kids' sake, 
parents can't always come home!

00:19:03.680 --> 00:19:06.360
I guess no one can go 
up against Mitama-san.

00:19:15.720 --> 00:19:17.660
Do you feel okay?

00:19:17.660 --> 00:19:18.760
Huh?

00:19:21.250 --> 00:19:23.810
Do you want to play house with me?

00:19:34.960 --> 00:19:38.050
<i>They ended up inviting six friends, right?</i>

00:19:45.180 --> 00:19:49.320
Oh, well. It sounds like they did 
stay in the house, at least.

00:19:50.360 --> 00:19:51.670
I'm home.

00:19:53.500 --> 00:19:54.420
Oh!

00:19:54.820 --> 00:19:55.890
Nee-nee!

00:19:57.670 --> 00:19:59.240
Welcome home!

00:19:59.240 --> 00:20:00.200
Thanks.

00:20:03.390 --> 00:20:06.550
You were playing with Sue-chan? Thank you.

00:20:06.550 --> 00:20:08.630
Oh, Nee-chan, welcome home!

00:20:09.620 --> 00:20:14.610
I'm home... and you three made 
someone else look after Sue-chan!

00:20:14.610 --> 00:20:16.690
We stayed home, didn't we?

00:20:16.690 --> 00:20:17.640
Hmph!

00:20:18.170 --> 00:20:21.420
We're hungry. Get us something to eat.

00:20:21.420 --> 00:20:23.900
Right, right. Bring everyone in.

00:20:24.740 --> 00:20:26.050
Thanks.

00:20:26.290 --> 00:20:27.400
Here.

00:20:27.400 --> 00:20:28.370
Thanks

00:20:28.370 --> 00:20:29.290
Huh?

00:20:29.290 --> 00:20:30.160
What's wrong?

00:20:30.160 --> 00:20:33.170
<b>Cold</b>

00:20:30.160 --> 00:20:33.170
<b>Ice Cream</b>

00:20:30.160 --> 00:20:33.170
<b>Ultra Vanilla</b>

00:20:31.220 --> 00:20:32.850
Nothing.

00:20:33.170 --> 00:20:36.170
<b>Mitama</b>

00:20:34.590 --> 00:20:36.160
Be careful getting home.

00:20:36.890 --> 00:20:38.520
Bye-bye!

00:20:41.970 --> 00:20:43.790
I'm home.

00:20:43.790 --> 00:20:44.920
It's Dad!

00:20:47.370 --> 00:20:49.160
Welcome home!

00:20:49.160 --> 00:20:50.770
Have you been good girls?

00:20:51.460 --> 00:20:54.190
Uh-huh! We stayed here 
and watched the house!

00:20:54.190 --> 00:20:56.590
But something weird happened.

00:20:57.270 --> 00:21:00.100
We brought six friends over to play.

00:21:00.100 --> 00:21:03.360
There were six playing 
detective tag with us,

00:21:03.610 --> 00:21:07.110
but one more was playing 
house with Sue-chan.

00:21:07.810 --> 00:21:11.970
Six plus one can't equal six, right?

00:21:12.570 --> 00:21:14.950
Didn't someone just show up late?

00:21:14.950 --> 00:21:18.110
No, nobody came that we didn't invite,

00:21:18.110 --> 00:21:20.290
and nobody left early.

00:21:20.770 --> 00:21:24.340
Maybe a zashiki warashi found 
her way into the group.

00:21:24.970 --> 00:21:26.630
Zashiki warashi?

00:21:26.930 --> 00:21:29.510
It's a supernatural being 
that takes a child's form.

00:21:29.510 --> 00:21:31.640
Supernatural? Like a ghost?

00:21:32.850 --> 00:21:35.780
It's a nice ghost. 
There's no reason to be scared.

00:21:35.780 --> 00:21:37.890
They bring good fortune.

00:21:38.310 --> 00:21:40.310
Still... a ghost?

00:21:41.190 --> 00:21:43.240
You had fun playing, didn't you?

00:21:44.390 --> 00:21:45.420
Yeah...

00:21:45.770 --> 00:21:47.090
Then what's the problem?

00:23:31.970 --> 00:23:35.970
<b>Next Time</b>

00:23:31.970 --> 00:23:35.970
<b>Why Are We So Bewildered When 
We Receive a Love Letter?</b>

00:23:31.970 --> 00:23:35.970
<b>You Can Tell What Type a Person Is by 
Whether They Believe in UMAs and UFOs or Not.</b>
